  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#usesConventionModel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#RoadSign"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#ConventionSignModel"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Relates a road sign class to the corresponding Vienna Convention sign model, family, or model variant.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Property characteristic added: this property is functional because a modelled sign variant should normally refer to one primary Vienna Convention model.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Aligned version: existing Vienna road-sign hierarchy extended with MTDS dataset classes, subclass axioms, and conservative exact owl:equivalentClass mappings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Refined MTDS alignment: MTDS dataset classes are connected to the road-sign hierarchy. owl:equivalentClass is reserved for one-to-one, high-confidence semantic matches; dataset-specific visual variants are mapped with rdfs:subClassOf to avoid over-strong logical equivalence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>This enrichment adds conservative OWL property characteristics and rdfs:comment definitions for the main road-sign and MTDS-aligned hierarchy classes without changing the existing hierarchy, equivalence axioms, object properties, or data properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Reasoning-oriented shape restrictions were added so that competency questions about shapes associated with traffic sign categories can be answered using Owlready2 and DL queries.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#hasSymbolCode">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#RoadSign"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Code or identifier for the symbol displayed on a road sign, when represented separately from the sign code.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/vienna-road-signs#ApproachToLevelCrossingOrSwingBridgeAdditionalSign">
